Android engine and native dependencies
---------------------------------------
The microWakeWord JNI/C++ integration is adapted from Home Assistant Android
at 110809fb146429a613cabeaa0eb2165be57939b9, Apache-2.0.
Project: https://github.com/home-assistant/android
Attribution: Home Assistant Android contributors. Upstream license is packaged
as Home-Assistant-Android-LICENSE.txt. Hermes adaptations include its package,
logging, asset/lifecycle integration and build wiring; these are not upstream
unmodified source. Preserve source headers and change notices when vendoring.

The native build uses TensorFlow Lite Micro (TFLM) and its algorithmic
microfrontend, KissFFT, FlatBuffers, gemmlowp and ruy. Their exact source
commits, archive hashes and license sources are recorded in
NATIVE-DEPENDENCIES.txt and inventory.json. Apache-2.0 full texts and upstream
attribution files are bundled. KissFFT requires BSD-3-Clause, including Mark
Borgerding's copyright; BOTH its COPYING notice and full LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause
text are packaged. COPYING alone is not the full BSD license.

